---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Header from "../../components/Header.astro";
import Footer from "../../components/Footer.astro";
const lang = "en";
const schema = [
  {
    "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
    "itemListElement": [
      {
        "@type": "ListItem",
        "position": 1,
        "name": "Lilo",
        "item": "https://getlilo.app/"
      },
      {
        "@type": "ListItem",
        "position": 2,
        "name": "Moving to Lilo",
        "item": "https://getlilo.app/moving/"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@type": "FAQPage",
    "@id": "https://getlilo.app/moving/#faq",
    "url": "https://getlilo.app/moving/",
    "inLanguage": "en",
    "mainEntity": []
  }
];
---
<Layout lang={lang} title="Switch to Lilo from Safari, Chrome, Arc or Firefox" description="Bring your bookmarks, open tabs, history, sign-ins and extensions to Lilo from Safari, Chrome, Arc, Firefox and eight more Mac browsers, in five minutes." schema={schema}>
<div class="top">
  <Header lang={lang} />

  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <svg class="mark bloom" viewBox="112 112 800 800" role="img" aria-label="Lilo logo">
        <use href="#petal-4"/><use href="#petal-3"/><use href="#petal-2"/><use href="#petal-1"/>
      </svg>
      <h1>Moving<br><span>to Lilo.</span></h1>
      <p class="sub">Lilo reads your bookmarks, tabs, history, sign-ins and extensions straight from the browsers on your Mac. Nothing leaves your Mac, and your other browser stays exactly as it was.</p>
      <div class="cta">
        <a class="pill dark" href="https://github.com/Alexays/Lilo/releases/latest/download/Lilo.dmg">Download for Mac</a>
        <a class="pill soft" href="#what">See what comes with you</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<main id="main-content">
  <section class="band" id="what">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="head">
        <span class="tag">What comes with you</span>
        <h2>Twelve browsers, read on your Mac.</h2>
        <p>Lilo finds every browser and every profile on this Mac, and lists first the one that opens your links today.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="matrix">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Browser</th><th scope="col">Bookmarks</th><th scope="col">Open tabs</th><th scope="col">History</th><th scope="col">Sign-ins</th><th scope="col">Extensions</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr><th scope="row">Safari</th><td class="y">Yes</td><td class="y">Last session</td><td class="y">Yes</td><td class="y">Yes</td><td class="n">No</td></tr>
            <tr class="grp"><th scope="rowgroup" colspan="6">Chromium browsers</th></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Chrome</th><td class="y">Yes</td><td class="y">Last session</td><td class="y">Yes</td><td class="y">Yes</td><td class="y">Yes</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Brave</th><td class="y">Yes</td><td class="y">Last session</td><td class="y">Yes</td><td class="y">Yes</td><td class="y">Yes</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Edge</th><td class="y">Yes</td><td class="y">Last session</td><td class="y">Yes</td><td class="y">Yes</td><td class="y">Yes</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Vivaldi</th><td class="y">Yes</td><td class="y">Last session</td><td class="y">Yes</td><td class="y">Yes</td><td class="y">Yes</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Opera</th><td class="y">Yes</td><td class="y">Last session</td><td class="y">Yes</td><td class="y">Yes</td><td class="y">Yes</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Arc</th><td class="y">Yes</td><td class="y">Spaces and tabs</td><td class="y">Yes</td><td class="y">Yes</td><td class="y">Yes</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Dia</th><td class="y">Yes</td><td class="y">Last session</td><td class="y">Yes</td><td class="y">Yes</td><td class="y">Yes</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Comet</th><td class="y">Yes</td><td class="y">Last session</td><td class="y">Yes</td><td class="y">Yes</td><td class="y">Yes</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Chromium</th><td class="y">Yes</td><td class="y">Last session</td><td class="y">Yes</td><td class="y">Yes</td><td class="y">Yes</td></tr>
            <tr class="grp"><th scope="rowgroup" colspan="6">Firefox browsers</th></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Firefox</th><td class="y">Yes</td><td class="y">Last session</td><td class="y">Yes</td><td class="y">Yes</td><td class="n">No</td></tr>
            <tr><th scope="row">Zen</th><td class="y">Yes</td><td class="y">Last session</td><td class="y">Yes</td><td class="y">Yes</td><td class="n">No</td></tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <div class="feat-list two">
        <div><b>Bookmarks.</b> The bookmarks bar becomes pinned tabs in your Space. Every other bookmark goes into one folder, and a folder inside a folder becomes its own folder, named by its path.</div>
        <div><b>Open tabs.</b> The tabs of your last Safari, Firefox, Zen or Chromium browser session open in your Space, one window after the other. From Chrome and the other Chromium browsers, pinned tabs stay pinned and each tab group becomes a folder with its name and color. From Arc, each space comes in as a Lilo Space with its icon and color, its pinned and open tabs, folders and splits of up to four tabs. Arc favorites become bookmarked tabs.</div>
        <div><b>History.</b> Up to your 50,000 most recent pages, so the command bar knows the sites you visit.</div>
        <div><b>Sign-ins.</b> Cookies are copied, so you stay signed in to your sites. Expired ones are left out.</div>
        <div><b>Extensions.</b> The ones from the Chrome Web Store are installed again from the store, up to date. You pick which.</div>
        <div><b>Profiles.</b> The first profile you pick lands in your current Space. Each other one gets its own Lilo profile and Space, so its sign-ins stay apart. Extensions go to the first one.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band" id="steps">
    <div class="wrap steps">
      <div class="head" style="margin:0">
        <span class="tag">The steps</span>
        <h2>A few clicks, then you are home.</h2>
        <p>Import is part of the welcome tour. Skip it and come back whenever you like.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="claims">
        <div class="claim"><span class="ic" style="background:#b39df4">1</span><div><h3>Pick your browser</h3><p>On first launch, "Bring your favorites" lists the browsers on your Mac. Pick one, or open "Choose what to import" to select profiles, data and extensions.</p></div></div>
        <div class="claim"><span class="ic" style="background:#9ac7eb">2</span><div><h3>Say yes to macOS</h3><p>For a Chromium browser, macOS asks to let Lilo use its "Safe Storage" key, to read your sign-ins: click Allow. Safari needs Full Disk Access, one switch in System Settings.</p></div></div>
        <div class="claim"><span class="ic" style="background:#9bd3b4">3</span><div><h3>Import again anytime</h3><p>Settings, General, Import from another browser. Running it again adds only what is new: links already in a Space and pages already in your history are not doubled.</p></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band" id="left">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="head">
        <span class="tag">What stays behind</span>
        <h2>Some things are better left where they are.</h2>
        <p>Lilo only reads what it needs and changes nothing in your other browser.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="shields two">
        <div class="shield"><span class="sic" style="background:#f4bb8c"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="5" y="10" width="14" height="10" rx="2"/><path d="M8 10V7a4 4 0 0 1 8 0v3"/></svg></span><div><h3>Passwords and cards</h3><p>Lilo never reads them and keeps no passwords itself. They stay in your password manager or iCloud Keychain, and setup offers to add your manager's extension.</p></div></div>
        <div class="shield"><span class="sic" style="background:#92a8ff"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M10 3h4v3a2 2 0 1 0 4 0h3v5h-3a2 2 0 1 0 0 4h3v6H3v-6h3a2 2 0 1 0 0-4H3V6h3a2 2 0 1 0 4 0z"/></svg></span><div><h3>Extension data</h3><p>Extensions arrive fresh from the store, so sign in to them or set them up again. Safari and Firefox extensions are not Chrome extensions and do not come along.</p></div></div>
        <div class="shield"><span class="sic" style="background:#9bd3b4"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="4" width="8" height="16" rx="2"/><rect x="13" y="4" width="8" height="16" rx="2"/></svg></span><div><h3>Closed and private tabs</h3><p>Only the tabs still open in your last session come in, each at the page it shows. Closed tabs, back history, private windows and the browser's own pages are left out.</p></div></div>
        <div class="shield"><span class="sic" style="background:#c3a5ea"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M3 12h18M12 3c2.5 2.7 2.5 15.3 0 18M12 3c-2.5 2.7-2.5 15.3 0 18"/></svg></span><div><h3>Site data beyond cookies</h3><p>Site permissions, local storage and form data are not copied. A site that keeps you signed in with more than a cookie may ask you to sign in once.</p></div></div>
        <div class="shield"><span class="sic" style="background:#e8d98f"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 3h12v18l-6-4-6 4z"/></svg></span><div><h3>Reading List and other extras</h3><p>Safari's Reading List, and anything in Arc's sidebar that is not a tab, a folder or a split, are skipped. Only web links (http and https) come in, and local files from a Chromium session.</p></div></div>
        <div class="shield"><span class="sic" style="background:#f0a8c8"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="22" height="22" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="3"/><path d="M12 2v3M12 19v3M2 12h3M19 12h3M4.9 4.9 7 7M17 17l2.1 2.1M4.9 19.1 7 17M17 7l2.1-2.1"/></svg></span><div><h3>Settings</h3><p>Search engine, downloads, themes and other preferences are not read. Set them once in Lilo's Settings.</p></div></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band" id="tips">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="head">
        <span class="tag">Feel at home</span>
        <h2>Your first week in Lilo.</h2>
        <p>A few things worth setting up once you have moved in.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="move">
        <div class="mv" style="background:#e8d98f"><h3>Keep your shortcuts</h3><p>Settings, General, Shortcuts. Start from the Lilo or the Arc preset, then remap anything. Conflicts are flagged as you type.</p></div>
        <div class="mv" style="background:#b39df4"><h3>A profile per Space</h3><p>Give Work and Perso their own profile, with their own cookies and extensions, side by side in one window.</p><div class="keys"><kbd>⌃1</kbd><kbd>⌃2</kbd></div></div>
        <div class="mv" style="background:#f0a8c8"><h3>Little window</h3><p>A quick window from any app, for one link or one search. Send it to a Space when it turns into something.</p><div class="keys"><kbd>⌘⌥N</kbd></div></div>
        <div class="mv" style="background:#9ac7eb"><h3>Peek</h3><p>Links from pinned tabs open over the page. Shift-click any link to peek at it.</p><div class="keys"><kbd>⇧ click</kbd></div></div>
        <div class="mv" style="background:#8fd5cf"><h3>Link rules</h3><p>Settings, General, Links from other apps. Send this domain to Work, the rest to the Little window.</p></div>
        <div class="mv" style="background:#f4bb8c"><h3>Command bar</h3><p>Your imported history and bookmarks are one search away, with tabs and every action.</p><div class="keys"><kbd>⌘T</kbd></div></div>
        <div class="mv" style="background:#9bd3b4"><h3>Your password manager</h3><p>Setup offers the one you use, such as Bitwarden, 1Password, Proton Pass, Dashlane, NordPass or KeePassXC.</p></div>
        <div class="mv" style="background:#c3a5ea"><h3>Open links in Lilo</h3><p>Make Lilo your default browser in Settings, so links from Mail and Slack land here.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band" id="faq">
    <div class="wrap faq">
      <div class="head" style="margin:0">
        <span class="tag">Questions</span>
        <h2>About switching.</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-list">
        <details><summary>Will my other browser change?</summary><p>No. Lilo only reads its files and writes nothing back. Its bookmarks, its sync and its passwords stay as they are, so you can keep it around as long as you like.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Do I need to quit it first?</summary><p>No. Lilo copies its databases before reading them, along with changes the running browser has not written out yet.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Why does macOS ask about "Safe Storage"?</summary><p>Chromium browsers encrypt their cookies with a key kept in your keychain. Lilo needs that key to keep you signed in. If you say no, everything else still imports.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Why does Safari need Full Disk Access?</summary><p>macOS protects Safari's folder. Lilo shows an "Allow access" button that opens the right page in System Settings, and finds Safari again when you come back.</p></details>
        <details><summary>I have several profiles. What happens?</summary><p>Each one is listed. The first you pick fills your current Space; each other one gets its own Lilo profile and Space, named after it. Importing the same profile again reuses them.</p></details>
        <details><summary>Some of my extensions did not come.</summary><p>Lilo reinstalls extensions from the Chrome Web Store only, and runs Manifest V3. Extensions installed by hand are left out, and Manifest V2 ones or the few that need Chrome-only features do not install. The <a href="https://github.com/Alexays/Lilo/blob/main/COMPATIBILITY.md">compatibility notes</a> list what differs.</p></details>
        <details><summary>What about sync and my phone?</summary><p>Lilo has no sync and no mobile app. Your other browser and your password manager keep syncing to your phone as before, since importing changes nothing in them.</p></details>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band">
    <div class="wrap end">
      <span class="tag">Free and open source</span>
      <svg class="mark" viewBox="112 112 800 800" aria-hidden="true" style="width:72px"><use href="#petal-4"/><use href="#petal-3"/><use href="#petal-2"/><use href="#petal-1"/></svg>
      <h2>Ready to move in?</h2>
      <p>Download Lilo, pick your browser, and your things are there in a few minutes.</p>
      <div style="display:flex;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;justify-content:center">
        <a class="pill dark" href="https://github.com/Alexays/Lilo/releases/latest/download/Lilo.dmg" style="padding:14px 22px">Download for Mac</a>
        <a class="pill soft" href="/" style="padding:14px 22px;background:color-mix(in srgb, var(--tint) 30%, var(--surface))">Back to Lilo</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer lang={lang} />
</main>
</Layout>
